From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: shrink TransparentBlt sources by whole pixels

Purpose: keep colour-keyed theme images intact when drawn smaller than
their source.
Wine before: TransparentBlt changed the stretch mode of the source DC, but
StretchBlt uses the destination's. The new work DC kept BLACKONWHITE, so
dropped rows and columns were ANDed into the copy: the 99x33 Luna Start
image drawn 30 pixels high got colours in neither row (439543 & 3f9640 =
039440).
XP behavior: keeps whole source rows (13, 15 and 17 for this size).
Change: select COLORONCOLOR in the work DC.
Evidence: tests/transparent-shrink.c checks with self-authored pixels that
every output pixel comes from the source or the untouched destination.
Scope: every Wine application.
Old patches: 0045.
---
 dlls/win32u/bitblt.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c b/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
index 48c76ba..9aaeaf9 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
@@ -856,7 +856,7 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtGdiTransparentBlt( HDC hdcDest, int xDest, int yDest, int widthDes
     COLORREF oldForeground;
     int oldStretchMode;
     DIBSECTION dib;
-    DC *dc_src;
+    DC *dc_src, *dc_work;
 
     if(widthDest < 0 || heightDest < 0 || widthSrc < 0 || heightSrc < 0) {
         TRACE("Cannot mirror\n");
@@ -890,6 +890,15 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtGdiTransparentBlt( HDC hdcDest, int xDest, int yDest, int widthDes
     }
     else bmpWork = NtGdiCreateCompatibleBitmap( hdcDest, widthDest, heightDest );
     oldWork = NtGdiSelectBitmap(hdcWork, bmpWork);
+    /* StretchBlt uses the destination DC's mode. A new DC starts with
+     * BLACKONWHITE, which ANDs the removed rows and columns of a shrunk image
+     * into colours that are neither the key nor the image. Sample whole
+     * source pixels, as Windows does for a colour-keyed stretch. */
+    if ((dc_work = get_dc_ptr( hdcWork )))
+    {
+        dc_work->attr->stretch_blt_mode = COLORONCOLOR;
+        release_dc_ptr( dc_work );
+    }
     if (!NtGdiStretchBlt( hdcWork, 0, 0, widthDest, heightDest, hdcSrc, xSrc, ySrc,
                           widthSrc, heightSrc, SRCCOPY, 0 ))
     {
